  "content": {
    "id": "p66-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Find values of $m$ for which the quadratic equation $x^{2}-2mx+9=0$ has real and different roots.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Real distinct roots require $\\Delta>0$: $m<-3$ or $m>3$.",
      "worked": "Real and different roots require $\\Delta>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-2m)^{2}-4(1)(9)\\\\&=4m^{2}-36\\\\4m^{2}-36&>0\\\\m^{2}-9&>0\\\\(m-3)(m+3)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe parabola $y=m^{2}-9$ opens upwards with intercepts $-3$ and $3$. It is above the axis outside these intercepts.\n$$m<-3\\quad\\text{or}\\quad m>3$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
